        "heading": "The control this claim intake callbacks needs",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A claim intake callbacks control starts with the loss report or claim event that opened the file. The assistant may collect the source, check the approved claims rule, and write the open question. The adjuster or claims owner keeps every decision that changes coverage, a payment, a denial, or a policyholder commitment. Virtual Claims Assistant places that boundary beside the claim intake callbacks queue so a new assistant does not borrow authority from an earlier claim. Any missing coverage evidence is marked missing until the source arrives.",
          "The common gap in claim intake callbacks is a record that looks current while the source document is absent. A claim file can move even when the policy page, the photo, or the vendor estimate is missing. Record the source, the date observed, the claim reference, and the next action before the case advances. That habit lets a reviewer rebuild the file without a private conversation. The claim file keeps the policy reference, the source document, and the claims owner with the note."
        ]
